/** @mainpage Qore ncurses Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section ncursesintro ncurses Module Introduction

    The \c ncurses module provides terminal user interfaces for %Qore: colored text,
    keyboard and mouse input, overlapping panels, and reusable widgets. Its API wraps
    the system ncurses library and serializes terminal calls across threads.

    Choose the layer that fits your application:
    - <b>Direct terminal drawing:</b> @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session "Session" manages the terminal,
      @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window "Window" draws and reads input, and
      @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel "Panel" manages overlapping surfaces. Use these for dashboards
      or custom interfaces; start with @ref ncurses_quickstartguide "Quick Start".
    - <b>Widget applications:</b> @ref ncursesuiintro "NcursesUi" supplies lists, editable text,
      menus, dialogs, tables, a file browser, layout managers, and an event loop. See
      @ref ncurses_ui_widgetsguide "UI Widget Toolkit" for a complete application.
    - <b>Interactive consoles:</b> @ref ncursesrepluiintro "NcursesReplUi" supplies input editing,
      command history, and layout/scroll calculations. The included \c qrepl program combines
      these with the widget toolkit; see @ref ncurses_toolsguide "Tools and REPL Helpers".

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Ansi "Ansi" handles colored tool output, while
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::TestTerminal "TestTerminal" supports automated tests without an
    interactive terminal. Terminal operations participate in %Qore sandbox and interruption checks.
    This is the module's initial 1.0 release. License terms are included in \c COPYING
    in the source distribution.

    Load the binary API with <tt>%requires ncurses</tt>. A minimal program and its terminal
    cleanup are explained in @ref ncurses_quickstartguide "Quick Start".

    @section ncursesdocumentation Documentation

    - @anchor ncurses_quickstart @ref ncurses_quickstartguide "Quick Start": create a session, draw
      a greeting, handle input, and restore the terminal on both normal and exceptional exits.
    - @anchor ncurses_mouse @ref ncurses_mouseguide "Mouse Support": enable reporting, interpret
      coordinates and button masks, and handle mouse, keyboard, and resize events in one loop.
    - @anchor ncurses_styles @ref ncurses_stylesguide "Style System": combine foreground/background
      colors and attributes, preserve borders, and choose wrapping behavior, with a styled-screen example.
    - @anchor ncurses_ansi @ref ncurses_ansiguide "ANSI SGR Text": render colored output, measure
      display width, parse styled segments, and wrap text without counting escape sequences.
    - @anchor ncurses_ui_widgets @ref ncurses_ui_widgetsguide "UI Widget Toolkit": build a list/status
      application with layout, focus, a quit handler, and modal dialog callbacks.
    - @anchor ncurses_testing @ref ncurses_testingguide "Automated Testing": create a headless terminal,
      inject typed events, assert screen contents, and test widgets without timing-dependent input.
    - @anchor ncurses_tools @ref ncurses_toolsguide "Tools and REPL Helpers": run \c qrepl, learn its
      controls, and use the input-buffer and history APIs in your own console.
    - @anchor ncurses_examples @ref ncurses_examplesguide "Examples": run the supplied dashboard,
      panels, and threaded-input demos, and follow a complete overlapping-panel example.
    - @anchor ncurses_api @ref ncurses_apiguide "API Overview": find lifecycle, drawing, input,
      style, and refresh APIs, including an example of batching screen updates.
    - @anchor ncursesreleasenotes_link @anchor ncursesreleasenotes_intro
      @ref ncursesreleasenotes "Release Notes": module version history.

    @section ncursesqlibmodules Qore User Modules

    - @ref ncursesuiintro "NcursesUi": widget tree, layouts, event dispatch, focus management,
      standard controls, and Unicode-aware terminal text helpers.
    - @ref ncursesrepluiintro "NcursesReplUi": input editing with
      @ref NcursesReplUi::InputBuffer "InputBuffer", history with
      @ref NcursesReplUi::History "History", and
      @ref NcursesReplUi::LayoutCalc "LayoutCalc" / @ref NcursesReplUi::ScrollCalc "ScrollCalc" helpers.

    @section ncurses_threads Threading

    Terminal calls are serialized by a module-level recursive lock.
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::readEvent() "Window::readEvent()" releases that lock between
    input checks so other threads can draw. Use @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::withLock() "Session::withLock()"
    for a short group of related drawing operations; protect application-owned data separately.
    Stop background readers before closing the session. See @ref ncurses_examplesguide "Examples"
    for the threaded-input demo and @ref ncurses_apiguide "API Overview" for batched refreshes.
*/
